Generate {{ num_docs }} English texts where PII-looking dummy values and genuine PII appear together.

## Purpose
Measure semantic discrimination so the model does not simply trust labels or reject anything described as a sample.

## PII Tag Format
- `<PERSON>John Carter</PERSON>`
- `<ADDRESS>123 Market Street, San Francisco, CA</ADDRESS>`
- `<ORGANIZATION>Northwind Analytics LLC</ORGANIZATION>`
- `<DATE_OF_BIRTH>S40.5.10</DATE_OF_BIRTH>`
- `<BANK_ACCOUNT>Chase Bank Midtown Branch Checking 1234567</BANK_ACCOUNT>`

## Concrete Patterns

### 1. Dummy labels plus real values
- `Name: not provided. Address: hidden. But applicant is <PERSON>John Carter</PERSON>.`
- `Account: send later. Actual transfer target is <BANK_ACCOUNT>Chase Bank Midtown Branch Checking 1234567</BANK_ACCOUNT>.`
- `Location: online only. Delivery goes to <ADDRESS>44 Pine Road, Seattle, WA</ADDRESS>.`

### 2. Example / note traps
- `Example: <PERSON>Mia Lopez</PERSON> (real data)`
- `This is not a test record: <ADDRESS>88 River Ave, Austin, TX</ADDRESS>`
- `Not dummy: <DATE_OF_BIRTH>S40.5.10</DATE_OF_BIRTH>`

### 3. Negation context
- `<PERSON>Daniel Park</PERSON> not <PERSON>David Park</PERSON> is correct`
- `It did not reach <ADDRESS>205 Lake Street, Chicago, IL</ADDRESS>`
- `The active account is <BANK_ACCOUNT>Citibank West Branch Checking 3344556</BANK_ACCOUNT>, not the old one`

### 4. Untagged dummy examples
- `Name: placeholder`
- `Address: sample city`
- `DOB: 19XX-XX-XX`
- `Account: cash only`

## Output Format
- Separate each text with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`
- Each text should be 70-220 characters
- Every text must include both tagged real PII and untagged dummy values
